    "media:imagetext": "September 20,1926\nMr. Joseph J.Phillips\nRight of Way\nAgent\nCity \u0026 County of San Francisco\nSan Francisco, California\nDear Sir:-\nIn accordance with your request for a price on our\nland situated at Millbrae,\nwe beg leave to submit the following,\nproviding satisfactory financial terms can be arranged.\nWe will deliver this land to the City and County of\nSan Francisco to be used as a Municipal Air Port, for the sum\nof $1500. per acre, the area included in this agreement to be\nall of our land lying between the Pacific Gas and Electric\nCompany's High Tension Transmission Line Easement and our\neasement for cord purposes sixty ere in water,\na right-of-way\neasement for road\nalong the\nnorthwesterly and southeasterly boundaries.\nWe also agree that if satisfactory arrangements cannot\nbe made with the West Coast Porcelain Company for the use of\ntheir spur;, to include sufficient land for a spur track from\nthe present Southern Pacific Railroad to the proposed field\nat the price per acre mentioned above.\nIn the event that the City and County of San Francisco\ncould not make the full payment at this timethat the City and\nwe would consider\na proportion of deferred payments, provided\nCounty of San Francisco paid 6% interest on the deferred payments\nand ail taxes levied against the property.\nVery truly yours,\nBAYSIDE COMPANY\nBy.\nSecretary\nMale. sty\n1100\nSay el\nFrancisco\n337.76\n322. 6\n660.36.\nacu-\n3700 NAh.",
